orum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383272-are-abominations-still-a-thing-in-v5?p=1383410#post1383410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@hmmm. Actually, I thought the Tzimisce had been written out, but you raise a very good point. Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not at all. They show up multiple times in the Camarilla book, for example. We just don't have full rules for them yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T14:30:00-07:00","id":1383441,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24808_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24808\" data-vbnamecard=\"24808\">Draconis</a> thanks. Are the Old Clan still a thing, or do all the Tzimisce have Vicissitude now? I\u2019m really curious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T15:02:06-07:00","id":1383449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383272-are-abominations-still-a-thing-in-v5?p=1383441#post1383441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24808_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24808\" data-vbnamecard=\"24808\">Draconis</a> thanks. Are the Old Clan still a thing, or do all the Tzimisce have Vicissitude now? I\u2019m really curious.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The Old Clan&quot; is now an epithet of the Tzimisce in general (cf &quot;the Eldest&quot;), and people speculate that the bloodlines will have the same discipline spread now, like what happened to the Banu Haqim castes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T15:20:09-07:00","id":1383453,"title":"","content":"That\u2019s interesting. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T16:01:28-07:00","id":1383461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383272-are-abominations-still-a-thing-in-v5?p=1383410#post1383410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@hmmm. Actually, I thought the Tzimisce had been written out, but you raise a very good point. Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just because it's not in the core book doesn't mean it's written out, despite what you might hear people shrieking about.<br /> <br /> V5 was designed in large part for new players, and stuffing everything in the core book wasn't their design goal. <br /> <br /> As far as the Tzimisce, what we've seen has been less 'woo alien head crest fleshcraft!' but there has been very little shown. We have some inklings from Chicago that Vicissitude will be folded into Protean as powers (an NPC has Protean that she learned from a Tzimisce, and V5's design of removing redundancy) but that's about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T17:23:24-07:00","id":1383474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383272-are-abominations-still-a-thing-in-v5?p=1383277#post1383277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V5's pretty early in its life cycle, and W5 isn't out yet.<br /> <br /> Abominations don't exist in V5 <i>yet</i>, but that's not the same as saying they don't exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>V5 is a baby vamp; please give it a chance ;-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/337-joe","name":"Joe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar337_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T08:45:47-07:00","id":1383777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383272-are-abominations-still-a-thing-in-v5?p=1383449#post1383449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;The Old Clan&quot; is now an epithet of the Tzimisce in general (cf &quot;the Eldest&quot;), and people speculate that the bloodlines will have the same discipline spread now, like what happened to the Banu Haqim castes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a feeling we're going to see some payoff on the whole &quot;Dracula is still trying to destroy Kupala's physical form&quot; thing. The Old Clan schismed with the Fiends over Vicissitude and its feared contamination by [Tzimisce]/Kupala/both. I know the implication is that Vicissitude is basically a way that [Tzimisce] was planning to control his clan, but has that been confirmed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T22:40:49-07:00","id":1384108,"title":"","content":"Back in 2nd Edition when Players Guide to the Sabbat came out the schism was political, i.e. the Fiends being the younger revolutionaries who joined the Anarch Revolt and founded the Sabbat, and the Old Clan being the surviving elders who stayed in Eastern Europe where they'd always been. We might see a return to that if Vicissitude gets condensed into Protean and is no longer eating the clan both literally and on a meta level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}